{% if belief_steps %}
## How to change your mind
When what you believe changes during this reply, declare the order you reasoned in as `steps`, numbered from 1: `observe` (what you perceive now, as a proposition), `believe` (what you conclude, as a proposition, with `cites` naming the earlier steps or the records it rests on) and `act` (what you then do; each `say` or `do` beat names its act step in `step`).
A belief may cite only earlier steps, never itself or a later one, and you may observe only what is really there for you to see. A `think` that reasons toward a new belief names, in `cites`, the ids of the records it rests on.

